  "@type": "Capability",
  "critical": true,
  "critical_note": "In arid and semi-arid climates, irrigation is the difference between productive agriculture and subsistence failure; it extends cultivation beyond rainfall-dependent regions",
  "description": "Controlled delivery of water to crops via gravity-fed canals, furrow and basin systems, water-lifting devices (shaduf, Archimedes screw, Persian wheel, saqiya), and low-pressure drip distribution. Covers canal survey and construction, flow measurement (Manning's equation), water-lifting device selection, salinity management, and irrigation scheduling by crop growth stage. Excludes motorized pump systems which belong to Water Distribution.",
  "early_win": true,
  "early_win_note": "Simple diversion canals and shadufs can be built within weeks using hand tools, immediately extending the growing season and stabilizing yields against drought.",
